Subject: [PATCH 1/2] ARM: dts: declare Lumia 920 CPU cell sizes
Upstream-Source: https://github.com/UEFI-code/linux-6.6-lumia920
Upstream-Revision: 9872e9316212490b7db8e3371fa1d63bd3394cc5
License-Provenance: kernel COPYING; ARM CPU binding in the same pinned tree

Single-cell CPU reg values require explicit address/size cell metadata.
No memory, peripheral, regulator or GPIO mapping changes.

--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/lumia920.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/lumia920.dts
@@ -14,6 +14,8 @@
     interrupt-parent = <&intc>;
 
     cpus {
+        #address-cells = <1>;
+        #size-cells = <0>;
         cpu@0 {
             device_type = "cpu";
             compatible = "qcom,krait";
